diagnosis_text:
A thorough five-phase broad search found no fault anywhere in the dc_clos_bgp topology. The reachability test run at diagnostic start shows both pc_0_0 → pc_0_1 and the reverse path forwarding with 0% packet loss (2/2 packets, RTT ≈ 1.4 ms). The L2 snapshot confirmed all seven devices have clean interface identity with no down or missing interfaces. The infra sweep found no ACL drop rules, no static ARP poisoning, and correct addressing on all hosts. The BGP snapshot shows leaf_router_0_1 — the alleged "rack top switch" — with both bgpd sessions in Established state, one to spine_router_0_0 (eth0) and one to spine_router_0_1 (eth1); an Established BGP session requires a live TCP connection over the physical link, which definitively disproves the claim that both uplinks are down. All five FRR routers have watchfrr, zebra, and bgpd running and healthy. The tc snapshot shows standard fq_codel qdiscs on all 16 interfaces with no shaping or corruption. The pressure sweep reports no stressed or suspect device. The link history for leaf_router_0_1 records zero network_down events and no historical flap evidence. The helpdesk report ("both uplinks cut off") is unconfirmed by any observable mechanism or trace. Root cause: no fault exists in the current lab state; the reported symptom either resolved before this diagnostic session began or was misattributed. No corrective action is needed.
=== END ===